	abstract = {The incorporation of photovoltaic (PV) systems into modern power grids necessitates efficient energy conversion architectures to enhance power extraction, voltage regulation, and overall system performance. Therefore, this research work presents a novel High Voltage Extended Boost (HVX-B) Converter to achieve ultra-voltage gain. A Coyote Optimised Radial Basis Function Neural Network (RBFNN) Maximum Power Point Tracking (MPPT) algorithm is implemented to dynamically track and extract maximum available power, ensuring optimal PV utilisation under erratic conditions. Additionally, a Bidirectional DC-DC Converter is introduced to manage energy flow over battery and the DC bus, improving system stability and power management. To enable seamless grid integration, a Three-Phase Voltage Source Inverter (VSI), controlled by a Proportional-Integral (PI) controller is used which regulates active and reactive power injection, ensuring voltage stability and power quality. The proposed system is validated through extensive MATLAB/Simulink simulation for accomplishing higher voltage gain, converter efficiency of 97.5%, tracking efficiency of 99.9%, standard deviation of 0.10 and improved dynamic response compared to conventional topologies. These outcomes show enhanced power conversion efficiency, improved grid stability and superior dynamic performance, making it an optimal solution for PV-grid applications. © 2026 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.},
