	abstract = {With the rapid expansion of photovoltaic power generation, achieving high-precision short-term forecasting for PV power plants has become increasingly critical for grid stability. As the scale of photovoltaic power generation expands, it becomes increasingly important to achieve high-precision short-term forecasting for photovoltaic power plants. However, traditional sequence forecasting methods exhibit significant limitations in capturing long-term dependencies and complex feature interactions. To address these challenges, this paper proposes a novel hybrid ensemble forecasting framework, BiGRU-LightGBM, which integrates bidirectional gated recurrent units (BiGRU) with a lightweight gradient boosting machine (LightGBM). The proposed model leverages BiGRU to extract temporal context features from sequential data, which are subsequently concatenated with original input features and processed through LightGBM for nonlinear regression prediction. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed model achieves superior performance with an R<sup>2</sup> of 0.7913 and MAE-M of 0.1176, significantly outperforming baseline models including RF, XGBoost, and LSTM networks. The results validate that the BiGRU-LightGBM framework exhibits excellent fitting capability and generalization performance, providing robust support for renewable energy power scheduling and grid integration applications. © 2025 IEEE.},
