	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105036056256?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Securing cyber-physical systems (CPS), which often form a nation's critical infrastructure, is becoming increasingly challenging. New threats are arising due to vulnerabilities in the Information Technology (IT), Operational Technology (OT), and their interactions. Moreover, the growth in artificial intelligence (AI) technologies have made it easy for attackers to exploit system vulnerabilities. A primary concern is the insufficient effectiveness of cyber operations and automated decision-making processes, which currently rely heavily on manual evaluation and subject matter experts (SMEs). A primary concern is the limited effectiveness of security evaluation methodologies in understanding a system's behavior during an attack. Current methodologies are generally suited for IT environments and do not easily adapt to OT due to their complexity. In addition, cybersecurity evaluation methods in OT often depend on manual evaluation and subject matter experts (SMEs). This paper introduces a novel framework based on LLMs and AI planning to automate threat emulation, facilitating the evaluation of the cybersecurity posture of OT systems. The newly introduced 'Automated Threat Emulation Framework' integrates with MITRE ATT&CK for automatic execution of various Tactics, Techniques, and Procedures (TTPs) employed by the real-time attacks for emulating the threats. Our framework employs multiple specialized LLM-driven agents that collaboratively perform tasks of context summarization, strategic planning, decision-making, external data retrieval, automated code generation, and secure execution. Central to our methodology is the incorporation of AI Planning and Causal Loop Diagrams (CLD) to accurately simulate cyber-attacks and systematically analyze cascading effects across interconnected CPS components. Through a comprehensive prototype implementation and a detailed case study involving a digital substation automation system, we demonstrate the practical effectiveness and robustness of our approach. Our research contributes significantly to the domain by providing a systematic, adaptive, and scalable solution for real-time cyber security threat assessment, enhancing the resilience and security posture of critical CPS infrastructure against emerging threats. © 2025 IEEE.},
