	doi = {10.1016/j.measurement.2024.115383},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85200272812?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Oil-immersed transformer is an important equipment of the power system with superior insulation performance and good cooling effect, so it is widely used in the power system. Temperature prediction of oil-immersed transformers is of great significance in the monitoring of transformer operation status and guiding power grid operation. Firstly, this paper describes the definition, classification, and significance of temperature prediction of oil-immersed transformers. In this paper, the temperature prediction of transformers is categorized into two types, which are the current hot-spot temperature prediction of the transformer and the future temperature prediction of the transformer. After that, the main research methods are introduced respectively. The methods for predicting the current hot-spot temperature of the transformer mainly include the prediction method based on thermal circuit model, the prediction method based on deep learning and the prediction method based on support vector machine. The methods for predicting the future temperature of the transformer mainly include the prediction method based on the LSTM neural network, the prediction method based on the similar day, and the prediction method based on the kernel extreme learning machine. The present paper describes the basic principles and key technologies of the above methods respectively, and analyzes the advantages, disadvantages, and limitations of various methods. In addition, the present paper summarizes the evaluation indexes of the current research methods and makes a comparative analysis of the current research methods. Finally, the present paper discusses three future research directions: comparing and contrasting different optimization algorithms to improve the hot-spot temperature prediction effect; establishing an integrated learning model based on random forest to improve the generalization degree and prediction accuracy of the model; and researching the prediction method of multi-model fusion, to obtain a better performance than the single-algorithm model. © 2024 Elsevier Ltd},
