	abstract = {This article investigates the application of artificial intelligence (AI) for optimizing wind energy systems through a combined theoretical, analytical, and practical approach. In the context of the global transition to renewable energy sources and the acute need to increase resource efficiency, AI-based solutions for managing and monitoring energy processes, as well as for predicting energy production, have become increasingly relevant. Instead of focusing on direct investments, the study presents a Python-based demonstration application designed to show how AI can improve the prediction and selection of certain solutions based on simple data such as the average wind speed in a given location. The tool simulates a realistic scenario involving a 30 MW wind farm, highlighting the benefit of AI in choosing the optimal technical solution based on the criterion of maximizing energy production. By integrating classical energy analysis with machine learning algorithms-in particular Random Forest-the application provides a working example of the potential of digitalization in the energy sector on a manageable scale. The educational and exploratory nature of the application provides a solid basis for more advanced future developments, which could be extended and integrated into energy systems around the world.  © 2025 IEEE.},
