	abstract = {In view of the problems of insufficient accuracy and low efficiency of traditional models in the evaluation of organizational effectiveness of power grid enterprises due to high data dimensions and complex nonlinear relationships, this paper proposes a multi-level optimization model construction method based on the XGBoost algorithm to improve the accuracy and practicality of the evaluation. After preprocessing through data cleaning, standardization and multicollinearity test, the random forest feature importance ranking and Spearman correlation coefficient method are used for multi-level feature screening (finally retaining 22 core indicators), and then the Bayesian optimization algorithm is combined to adjust the hyperparameters of XGBoost (including optimizing max-depth to 7, reducing learning-rate to 0.03, and increasing n-estimators to 350), and the Stacking integration strategy is introduced to fuse the LightGBM and CatBoost models. The experimental results show that the optimized model achieves an accuracy of 95.3% on a test set containing 150,000 power grid enterprise operation data, and the key indicator MAE is reduced to 0.04. This model effectively solves the problem of dynamic evaluation of organizational effectiveness of power grid enterprises and provides reliable data support for resource optimization and allocation. © 2025 IEEE.},
