	abstract = {In this research, the authors introduce the step-by-step construction of an AI control system on Electric Vertical Take-Off and Landing (eVTOL) vehicles by means of Physics-Constrained Generative Adversarial Network (physicsGAN) coupled with a surrogate-based optimization algorithm. In PyTorch, the framework is implemented, which is smart enough to create optimum take-off control profiles, namely power and wing angle profiles and at the same time meet physical and operational limitations strictly. Surrogate models including LSTM networks to forecast time-series and DNN to estimate energy were trained based on highfidelity simulation data with an accuracy of more than 99.99 percent. The physicsGAN makes no use of postoptimization constraint reasoning, with its bounds fully respected by the physics-simulated layout space; it also makes optimization fast to execute with Differential Evolution. Comparative findings indicate a match of 99.6 percent against the simulation-based optimal solutions with the computing times decreased by an order of about 200 times. The proposed strategy would become an efficient, scalable, and robust solution towards real-time eVTOL controllability, thus of great importance to the field of safe and energy-efficient urban air mobility. © 2025 IEEE.},
