	abstract = {Accurate battery state of health (SOH) estimation is crucial for the reliable operation of renewable energy systems, enabling timely maintenance and failure prevention. This paper first introduces Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) and Temporal Convolutional Network (TCN) as meta-learners, Support Vector Regression (SVR) as a base learner, and Whale Optimization Algorithm (WOA) as a parameter optimizer. Then a novel WOA-GRU-TCN-SVR (WGTS) model is proposed for the SOH estimation of lithium-ion batteries through ingenious stacking. The combination of deep learning and traditional machine learning can enhance the inherent performance of the model. Besides, new original and generated health features (HFs) are extracted from the battery cycling data by analyzing the incremental capacity (IC) curve and voltage curve. A correlation analysis is conducted between HFs and battery SOH to identify highly correlated features for SOH estimation. Finally, the proposed WGTS model is trained using the selected HFs to effectively perform battery SOH estimation. Multiple comparative experimental results prove the accuracy and robustness of the proposed WGTS model in terms of the battery SOH estimation, which achieves the lowest Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE) and highest coefficient of determination (R-squared, R<sup>2</sup>) on the NASA and CALCE datasets compared with baseline models and conventional models. © 2025 Elsevier B.V.},
