	abstract = {This work presents the design and deployment of a smart, self-sustainable energy management system for a hybrid solar-wind microgrid aimed at rural or off-grid environments. The proposed system combines Internet of Things (IoT) technologies, MQTT-based communication, and a cloud-native architecture to enable real-time energy monitoring, remote load control, and intelligent decision support. A machine learning model (Random Forest) generates an estimation of daily renewable energy generation based on historical patterns, while a large language model (LLM) generates personalized natural language recommendations by analyzing recent consumption data and estimated energy production in the following days. The system autonomously controls electrical loads using smart plugs with Tasmota firmware, optimizing energy usage according to battery status and generation-consumption balance. With a transmission reliability of 98.46% and validated energy sustainability under varying weather conditions, the system has proven robust and operationally viable for off-grid contexts. While the energy estimation module does not predict short-term variations, it effectively supports user planning by highlighting daily generation trends. These results confirm the platform potential as a low-cost, scalable solution for intelligent microgrid management in rural or off-grid environments, using AI and IoT for sustainable development.  © 2025 IEEE.},
