	abstract = {This paper focuses on the balance control of distribution network outage plans, and conducts research based on the actual business needs of Yuexiu Power Supply Bureau of China Southern Power Grid. By collecting detailed data of 16 dimensions of outage plans in the past three years, after preprocessing, a machine learning algorithm is used to build an outage plan time prediction model, and the performance of random forest, support vector machine and neural network models is compared. Finally, the support vector machine model is selected and its parameters are optimized. The model accuracy after optimization reaches 89.32% and the MSE is 2.68. At the same time, various constraints affecting the outage plan scheduling are determined, and a balance index calculation algorithm is designed. In the experimental simulation, various outage scenarios are simulated, and the results show that the mechanism can effectively improve the balance of the outage plan. In the actual application of Yuexiu Power Supply Bureau, the change rate of 300 monthly balance indicators of the team in 2023 was only 6.7%, a year-on-year decrease of 78.6%, the number of continuous long-term operations of the team decreased by 87% year-on-year. The change rate of 15 of the 21 monitoring indicators decreased by more than 50%, the on-time start rate increased by 73%, and the delayed power transmission rate decreased by 65%. In addition, the annual project power transmission time was advanced by 1.5 hours, the number of power outage complaints decreased by 37%, and the time consumption of various projects decreased by an average of 1 hour year-on-year, indirectly reducing the loss of electricity bills by about 390,000 yuan, and the power supply time of the generator truck decreased by an average of 1.5 hours, saving about 100,000 yuan in costs. The research results provide an effective method for the management of distribution network power outage plans, significantly improving the reliabili