	abstract = {Offshore wind farms are essential for sustainable energy production but have maintenance difficulties owing to severe environmental conditions and restricted accessibility. This paper presents an innovative predictive maintenance framework using Random Forest algorithms to improve the operational dependability of autonomous offshore wind turbines. IoT-enabled sensors constantly gather data on essential factors like vibration, temperature, rotor speed, and acoustic signals from vital turbine components. The dataset, consisting of more than 1.2 million sensor readings from 150 turbines during a 12-month period, was used to train and verify the model. The Random Forest method achieved a fault classification accuracy of 96.3%, with a precision of 94.8% and a recall of 95.5%. The proposed solution decreased unscheduled downtime by 41% and prolonged component lifespan by 22% compared to conventional scheduled maintenance. Moreover, operating expenses decreased by 18%, mostly due to early fault identification and focused treatments. The findings illustrate the effectiveness of machine learning-based maintenance in offshore settings. The system optimizes decision-making, facilitates autonomous maintenance operations, and boosts energy production and asset durability in renewable energy systems. © 2025 IEEE.},
