	abstract = {A robust management of the aviation industry is closely related to providing an accurate and satisfactory forecasting model in order to achieve a balanced and mature aviation industry. With the aid of accurate forecasting projections, investors and managers in the aviation sector can create short-, medium-, and long-term roadmaps to determine investment and capacity expansion decisions. In the light of the mentioned issues, strategic and operational decisions such as the correct planning of domestic and international passenger capacities, the decision to purchase new aircraft, and the addition of a new flight route/new crews to expand the existing fleet team can be taken by airline managers. In this regard, an optimal and accurate forecasting study for the air transportation industry is an invaluable task to synchronize each connected workflow. The aim of this study is to forecast air passenger demands in aviation transport model of Turkey, one of the fastest emerging countries in the world, which has made significant progress in the aviation sector, employing traditional forecasting methods such as time series methods, multiple linear regression (MLR) and recently developed machine learning algorithms such as support vector machines (SVM), artificial neural networks (ANN) and random forest (RF) algorithms. In accordance with comparative studies, the intention is to show more reliable and accurate results in terms of lower prediction errors for each characteristic tool. The success of the performance of the developed model has been demonstrated using various case studies. It is expected that this study will help researchers working on this subject with its informative results and unique data structure in different time-periods. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Turan Paksoy and Sercan Demir. All rights reserved.},
