	abstract = {Smart grids are crucial in modern energy systems, integrating sensors, communication networks, and control mechanisms to improve energy distribution. However, conventional methods like Time-Based Scheduling (TBS), Demand Response Mechanism (DRM), and Static Load Distribution (SLD) struggle with inefficiencies such as poor real-time load balancing, limited adaptability, and inaccurate power usage predictions. These drawbacks hinder the overall effectiveness of smart grid systems.To address these challenges, the proposed AI-Driven Power Management System (AI-PMS) leverages machine learning to optimize energy distribution and predict demand more accurately. By using historical and real-time data, AI-PMS dynamically adjusts power flow, ensuring better load distribution and efficiency. This method surpasses the limitations of TBS, DRM, and SLD. The implementation of AI-PMS has resulted in a 0.25% improvement in energy efficiency and a 0.15% boost in grid reliability, significantly reducing power losses. The system also enhances the integration of renewable energy sources, making it a more sustainable and adaptive solution for modern smart grids. These advancements promise better power management and lower operational costs for grid operators. © 2024 IEEE.},
