	doi = {10.1007/978-981-99-0451-8_114},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85152631472?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Load prediction plays an important role in ensuring the safe and stable operation of the micro-grid power system. Traditional load prediction is mainly aimed at large power grids which different from the micro-grid. Traditional load prediction method has some defects, such as training sample selection, point prediction error and so on. This paper proposes a load interval prediction model of micro-grid based on Grey Wolf Optimization Least Squares Support Vector Machine (GWO-LSSVM). Firstly, load history data is preprocessed based on K-means clustering method; MIC is used to analyze the correlation of load characteristics, and the factors with high load influence are selected as input variables; Secondly, through the Grey Relational Analysis (GRA), the relationship between the characteristics is further analyzed, and the similar days are screened out; Then, combining GWO with LSSVM build the optimal model; Finally, error fitting by t distribution, then get interval of the predicted load. Based on the data of an actual industrial park, compares with Random Forest (RF), Multiple Linear Regression (MLR) and Artificial Neural Network (ANN). FE results show that the model is superior to others in RMSE, MAE, R<sup>2</sup>, and confirm the validity of the prediction. © 2023, Beijing Paike Culture Commu. Co., Ltd.},
