	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85124126123?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Single-phase asynchronous motor needs only a single-phase power supply in operation, which has the advantages of convenient operation, simple structure, and low cost. Widely used in household small power electrical appliances. However, the efficiency of single-phase asynchronous motors is generally low. The single-phase induction motor rotor adopts a copper strip-rotor, which can not only improve the efficiency of the motor but also avoid the problem of copper casting. However, it will make the starting torque of the motor smaller and the starting current larger. To solve this problem, and improved polyhedron algorithm is proposed to optimize the motor. Firstly, the Taguchi algorithm is used to reduce the dimension of the motor. Then, taking the starting torque multiple and the starting current multiple as targets, the objective function is determined by the response surface method. Finally, the regular polyhedron algorithm with weight coefficient is used to optimize the motor and the final optimization parameters of the motor are obtained. The results show that the algorithm can improve the optimization accuracy and the motor performance is more ideal. Finally, through the prototype production, the optimization effect is verified, which has a certain engineering significance. © 2021 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {Copper rotor single-phase asynchronous motor; Optimal design; Polyhedral method; Response surface method; Taguchi algorithm},
	keywords = {Efficiency; Electric power systems; Induction motors; Surface properties; Copper rotor single-phase asynchronoi motor; Copper rotors; Optimal design; Polyhedral method; Response surfaces methods; Single phase asynchronous motors; Single phase induction motor; Starting current; Starting torque; Taguchi algorithm; Geometry},
	type = {Conference paper},
